  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Fedora 6 breaks out resource representation into a number of small files for each resource.  The more versions of a resource you have, the more of these small files will be generated.   Compared to Fedora 3 , Fedora 6 uses many more files and therefore when running on linux,  many more inodes.  Depending on the structure of one’s Fedora 3 repository - ie if you have a large number of  versions on each resource - the migrated Fedora OCFL repo can have an order of magnitude more files.   ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Furthermore, when using the migration validator,  many small files are generated as part of the validation and reporting process.   ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The task here is to document how users should estimate the number of inodes they’ll need based on the number of resources they intend to store/migrate.  Also it would be good to highlight the migration validator options that can be used to minimize inode consumption.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
